HTTP Request and Response.
• What is the main difference between HTTP GET request and HTTP POST request?
• When to use HTTP GET request and when to use HTTP POST request?
• What does it mean for HTTP response status code 200, 301, and 404?


The main difference between HTTP GET AND POST request is the GET passes the information into the URL and POST passes the information through the body.
If you need to copy-n-paste information you should use GET. If you have sensitive information or large files/data then you should use POST.

200  means "ok" 
 301 means "move permanently" 
 404 means "file not found"

 